  "speechText": "I would not process a large file completely inside the API request. The API uploads the file to object storage and creates a job. A queue sends the job to a worker. The worker processes the file in smaller steps and updates the job status, for example queued, running, completed, or failed. For large jobs, I also use checkpoints so the worker can continue from the last successful step after a failure.",
